  "evidence": [
    {"key": "physics_elevator", "source": "physics_report", "segment_index": 3, "start_ms": 57722, "end_ms": 87950, "quote": "In that accelerated coordinate system, an isolated body would not move at constant velocity."},
    {"key": "physics_question", "source": "physics_report", "segment_index": 4, "start_ms": 87950, "end_ms": 118733, "quote": "What if the body is not isolated?"},
    {"key": "physics_two_points", "source": "physics_report", "segment_index": 5, "start_ms": 118733, "end_ms": 144871, "quote": "Now there are two important points I want to make about Newton's second law."},
    {"key": "physics_general", "source": "physics_report", "segment_index": 8, "start_ms": 208223, "end_ms": 240000, "quote": "So why do we talk about this as being the more general form?"},
    {"key": "physics_explanation", "source": "physics_report", "segment_index": 8, "start_ms": 208223, "end_ms": 240000, "quote": "It's because this second form of Newton's second law can be generalized to a system of particles or a system where mass is flowing and the mass of something is changing."},
    {"key": "biology_goal", "source": "biology_report", "segment_index": 1, "start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 40000, "quote": "So today we're going to continue with amino acids, peptides, and proteins, and I'm going to talk about a different protein variant that is the causative, the cause of sickle cell anemia, and it's a very interesting structural issue."},
    {"key": "biology_structure", "source": "biology_report", "segment_index": 2, "start_ms": 40000, "end_ms": 80000, "quote": "So last time we discussed how the primary sequence of a polypeptide chain defines its folded structure."},
    {"key": "biology_goal_return", "source": "biology_report", "segment_index": 4, "start_ms": 101825, "end_ms": 125903, "quote": "And when we talk about hemoglobin, which is the protein that has a problem, is the cause of sickle cell anemia, you'll see that that is a heterotetrameric protein."},
    {"key": "biology_definition", "source": "biology_report", "segment_index": 5, "start_ms": 125903, "end_ms": 154586, "quote": "But if you subject a protein to various treatments that may break up those weak forces, the protein will undergo a process of denaturation."},
    {"key": "biology_question", "source": "biology_report", "segment_index": 5, "start_ms": 125903, "end_ms": 154586, "quote": "So can anyone think of what kinds of things would cause protein denaturation? Yes."},
    {"key": "biology_responses", "source": "biology_report", "segment_index": 6, "start_ms": 154586, "end_ms": 186310, "quote": "Heat is a bad one, is a serious one, obviously. And heat, yes, I'll write them all down. What's here? PH, so PH, acidity, basicity, and we'll talk about why those things cause changes."},
    {"key": "biology_reform", "source": "biology_report", "segment_index": 7, "start_ms": 186310, "end_ms": 226310, "quote": "You're going to break those weak bonds and then they can either reform or if you go to too high heat, the unfolded protein starts to form aggregates."},
    {"key": "biology_egg", "source": "biology_report", "segment_index": 8, "start_ms": 226310, "end_ms": 240020, "quote": "Has ever scrambled an egg, knows that that is an irreversible process. You don't get to cram the egg back into the shell."},
    {"key": "biology_caption_heat", "source": "biology_captions", "start_ms": 154517, "end_ms": 155350, "quote": "AUDIENCE: Some heat."},
    {"key": "biology_caption_ph", "source": "biology_captions", "start_ms": 162700, "end_ms": 163887, "quote": "AUDIENCE: pH."}
  ],
